  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "zamgx97",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Introduction and Functions of OS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Operating Systems oversee system resources through core modules: Process, Memory, File, and I/O Management.",
        "Process Management includes thread allocation, state transitions, and execution scheduling using CPU Scheduling Algorithms.",
        "Process Synchronisation deals with concurrent execution risks, resolving the Critical Section Problem and preventing Deadlocks.",
        "Memory Management optimizes RAM utilization using Page Replacement Algorithms.",
        "I/O Systems and Disk Scheduling organize external storage access and minimize read/write seek time."
      ],
      "id": "999i4ke"
    },
