    {
      "id": "0xtwd5y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Page Replacement Algorithms"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "CPU Scheduling Algorithms (FCFS, SJF, Round Robin, Priority) are frequently tested for calculating average waiting and turnaround times.",
        "Deadlock conditions (Mutual Exclusion, Hold and Wait, No Preemption, Circular Wait) and Banker's Algorithm are high-yield exam topics.",
        "Page Replacement Algorithms (FIFO, LRU, Optimal) and Belady's Anomaly are recurring questions in competitive exams.",
        "Disk Scheduling algorithms (SSTF, SCAN, C-SCAN, LOOK) are consistently evaluated for head movement calculation."
      ],
      "id": "prcavnd"
    },
